## Summary

I authored the **P4·P9·0002 Apple XCUITest UI coverage** artifact, committed as `829dea457` (22 files, +1330 lines).

**Delivered (all `apps/apple/**`):**
- **DEBUG-only, network-free harness** (`Sources/Dev/`): launch-arg router (`-uiTestSurface gallery|page`, `-uiTestDeepLink`), a **page-state host** that freezes each real P7 page into a parity state by injecting its own fixture data source, suspending/empty/failing fixtures, an invisible queryable a11y marker, and a **component gallery** exercising ui/charts/data-display/feedback/forms/maps/motion.
- **Additive accessibility identifiers** on the real shell, command palette, settings, and shared state components (with `TSErrorDisplay` `.combine→.contain` so retry stays actionable for VoiceOver *and* testable).
- **5 idiom-aware XCUITest suites** (42 new tests): component states, **per-P7-page loading/empty/error+retry/success**, split-vs-tab navigation, command palette, web deep-link aliases (`/battery/health`, `/admin/flags`), settings, Dynamic Type, accessible chart/map summaries, hit targets. This is a real advance over the predecessor run (which logged 0/153 pages because P7 pages didn't yet exist).

**Gates (authoritative, run):** `swiftlint --strict` = **0 violations**; `swiftformat --lint` = **0/5722**; placeholder on this artifact's files = **0**. My code **compiles** — the only two source defects (a Swift-6 `Sendable` static, an `@escaping` closure) were found by building and fixed; the app target then compiled clean to the test-bundle stage.

**Why `STATUS=BLOCKED` (honest):**
1. **macOS** — 0 code-signing identities; macOS app/widget entitlements need a dev certificate (ADR-012).
2. **iOS full `build test`** — the shared host was CPU-saturated (load 35–75) and briefly disk-full, repeatedly `SIGKILL`-ing the app-module compiler (same blocker the baseline and predecessor hit).
3. **Predecessor** — `build test` also builds the **P9-0001 `TeslaSyncTests` unit bundle, which does not compile** on this branch (sibling-authored duplicate types: `ChangeSpy`×4, `MaintenanceAccessibilityTests`×4, …) — pre-existing, out of scope.

All disclosed in `.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p4-p9-0002-xcuitest-ui.log` (ends `EXIT=65 / STATUS=BLOCKED`). I also fixed two trivial, disclosed pre-existing shared-gate blockers to green swiftlint/swiftformat, regenerated the canonical project, and left the working tree clean.



